WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:03.680
A brand-new phone: nine hundred euros.

2
00:00:03.730 --> 00:00:07.310
Each year it loses twenty per
cent of what it's worth now.

3
00:00:07.360 --> 00:00:09.970
Nine hundred, then seven
hundred and twenty,

4
00:00:10.020 --> 00:00:12.620
then five hundred and seventy-six.

5
00:00:12.670 --> 00:00:16.890
Compare a phone that loses a fixed
one hundred and eighty euros a year.

6
00:00:16.940 --> 00:00:19.780
After five years, that one hits zero.

7
00:00:19.830 --> 00:00:21.860
So what about the first phone?

8
00:00:21.910 --> 00:00:24.110
Does it run out after five years too?

9
00:00:24.160 --> 00:00:25.150
After ten?

10
00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:26.280
Or never?

11
00:00:26.330 --> 00:00:30.710
In this mission, you'll see that losing
twenty per cent means multiplying by nought

12
00:00:30.760 --> 00:00:32.880
point eight, every year.

13
00:00:32.930 --> 00:00:36.090
A constant multiplier
gives an exponential model.

14
00:00:36.140 --> 00:00:38.730
A constant amount gives a linear one.

15
00:00:38.780 --> 00:00:42.610
Your mission: decide whether
the phone is ever worth nothing.
